Sval: paint every color a frame resolves through its site style

A site style tints and inverts a page's colors as they are painted
(chrome/layout/style/SvalSiteStyleColors.cpp, ported from Zen Browser's
boosts backend). A user sheet can only replace colors, and a filter on the
page inverts its pictures with it. StyleAbsoluteColor::ToColor is where
every computed color becomes an nscolor, so it takes the frame the color is
painted for and applies the frame's document's style there. The frame
argument defaults to null, which leaves a color as it is, so only the
callers that paint a frame's colors pass one: nsIFrame's and
ComputedStyle's GetVisitedDependentColor, CalcColor, ToDeviceColor for
gradient stops, and the canvas's default background.

